{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792830721,"nonce":"9YLDUNow8NYf/w9egoytS/09P3Y=","title":"Compiler: no exact struct type reaches the optimiser for Python programs","message":"Python marks its leaf classes exact (EXACT_STRUCT_KEY), and LICM, load CSE and the typed alias check read exact types from module.types by name. For a Python program module.types holds none of them: record_exact_struct_types drops any exact type whose name another registered type shares, and every Python class, the builtin exceptions included, is in the lowering registry twice under one name with two type ids (Array2D as 30 and 49) and one layout. A temporary trace in LICM on sor_plain.py showed 13 exact ids, 0 types, an empty exact set.\n\nEffect: LICM cannot tell an instance field from a store through a list's element storage, so a loop over self.data[...] reads self's fields and the list header again on every access.","files":null}]}